A||||18||Alex4mula||Good things about our suppliers||||6||
Z||000000||Alex4mula||10-25-2001||11:16 AM||||It is very easy to talk about negatives and many times with good reasons. But in these times all we hear are a lot of bad news etc. and even here sometimes the negatives are more than the good ones in this area.<BR>I just wanted to share something good, or more specifically, something good and "unexpected" about a Fiero supplier.<BR>Couple week ago I bought a Rack & Pinion from the Fiero Store with a core charge of $100. When returning it I included another R&P that I took off 3 years ago (other car) when I bought one from them. At that time I just couldn't return it so I stored it in a corner. I explained this to them and to my surprise they reimbursed me $180!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> They didn't have to accept it and a $20 penalty for a 3yrs delay is OK for me. Also at that time the core charge was $50. So, do you have any good story?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red-Original Owner & White-1/94 with PM (:||||reg||6
Z||000001||MinnGreenGT||10-25-2001||11:24 AM||||Rodney Dickman rules!  I've ordered a few small parts from him- they always show up within 2 days (he's in Wisconsin). Also very quick in correspondence.<P>FieroDave- ordered two sets of wing-studs from him (off ebay), and he sent three! He always promptly answers his email and is a general pleasure to work with.<P>TheFieroStore- ordered a heater core and a low-temp thermostat... fast shipping, and quick emails too!<P>Hmmm.... Archie- but I haven't ordered from him. He's just cool.<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroBUZZ||10-25-2001||11:31 AM||||Living in Canada can be a PITA with shipping and all.  I got Sage's scoops through 007DOUG with great service. A super product as well.<P>The big brown truck just brought me a TB and plenum from Darrell Morse an hour ago. Another super guy to deal with.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>Gary||||reg||6
Z||000003||TRiAD||10-25-2001||11:47 AM||||Well, I haven't bought anything from anyone yet, but...<P>I have been to Archie's, and I can tell you he was more than accomodating (and patient) with me and my little brother.<P>I also have been dealing with Pat (ferrari_momo) via email a LOT lately, and I can tell you he's VERY prompt with his communication. <P>So far I have been impressed with The Fiero Store every time I've talked with them, and as soon as my GT gets here (next weekend!) I'll be placing my first order with them. <P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg"> <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Fformula88||10-25-2001||12:37 PM||||So far I have dealt with Bob Steiger at Twin Lakes, Kick Hill farms, and The Fiero Store, both with great results!<P>Fiero Bob is great to do business with!  He found me a great set of quarter windows with the SE on them, and although I am not positive on what he charged me it wasn't more than like $30 or so per.  Maybe less.  He also was willing to talk to me for what had to be at least an hour at the Columbus FOCOA event and even gave me a big discount on a factory wing!  Great guy!<P>No complaints with Kick Hill Farms either!  Quick service!  I got some mirrors from him, and although they needed repainting (I expected that and did not ask for pristine ones anyway) mechanically they worked perfectly!  He also sent me an engraved plenum for my 88 Fiero (long story why I needed a new one!) which looked nearly factory after I cleaned off the old oil/grease!<P>The Fiero store has been very accomodating.  On two occasions I had a problem with the order.  The first they sent a Fiero decklid decal to me which was the wrong one for my model (it was solid letters, I needed split).  Within two days I had a new one free of charge!  I also had ordered a radiator cap and got a reseviour cap.  Again, they shipped the correct part free of charge.  Both wrong parts were mine to keep too!  I like their service.<P>I have even ordered from the FOCOA store.  I wanted their embroidered floormats, and they sent me the wrong ones.  I wasn't too happy because it took a month to get them, but when I called they had the correct ones to me within a week (cross country too!).  So they were very willing to correct my problem.  They also gave me a small credit towards a future purchase or membership renewal.  All in all not bad.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Cheever3000||10-25-2001||12:37 PM||||Fiero Store - my car was in the shop and needed tranny mounts among other things.  The shop guys couldn't find any, but I found them on TFS website and called.  They sent them directly to the shop VERY quickly, and the price was great.<P>Rodney Dickman - I have only ordered low-cost items from him so far, but always got what I wanted, the quality I expected, good prices, and very fast shipping.<P>Except for things from individuals here on PFF, that's all the Feiro parts vendors I think that I've ever bought from.<BR>||||reg||14
Z||000006||BlackStang95||10-25-2001||12:42 PM||||At least with your suppliers you know them well and can keep track on who has the best of whatever.  Mustang parts are a pain, junkyards and many sites online charge exorbant rates.  Most of the time i end up buying from ford itself (and thats hardly cheap).  So...try to see the bright sides.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000007||stimpy||10-25-2001||01:10 PM||||Yep, stang, we're a tight little community. Kind of a Six Degrees of Fiero Nation thing. Everyone knows someone who has met some one etc. That's one of the great things about having a car that is part of a relatively small niche. So you can see why we are so protective of our little hang out here.<P>I want to second the positive things about Doug Kinney. I ordered a set of his tinted sail panels as "factory seconds". He gave me a great discount on account that they had a small chip on one (Totally invisible once monted) and did not discount one bit on his service. All emails returned very promptly, and he even delivered the part <B>before</B> I sent payment. Heckuva guy. <P>Also, kudos to The Fiero Store. I had been looking for a GT trunk weatherstripping. Lots of people "had em" at a cheaper price, but not in stock. With the rainy weather approaching, I put in my order with the Fiero Store, paid a bit more, but had my part within 48 hours||||reg||14
Z||000008||DRH||10-25-2001||01:14 PM||||Rodney Dickman and Fiero Store have both delivered quickly, accurately and with a great product.<P>Even though I haven't bought anything from him, I did stop by Ed Park's place a couple of years ago. Ed was gone on a parts run but his wife gave me a tour of the shop and turned me loose to just walk around the yard and look at all the parts cars. Very friendly and took a lot of time with someone that wasn't even buying anything. I wouldn't hesitate to do business with him.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Jefrysuko||10-25-2001||02:41 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by BlackStang95:<BR><B>At least with your suppliers you know them well and can keep track on who has the best of whatever.  Mustang parts are a pain, junkyards and many sites online charge exorbant rates.  Most of the time i end up buying from ford itself (and thats hardly cheap).  So...try to see the bright sides.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>You secretly want a fiero don't you?  Come on you can admit it.  Your among friends here.  We understand how it goes, your friend got a Fiero and you saw how much better it was than your car but you didn't want to admit it because you had been braging so much about your mustang.  Now if you admit that you want a Fiero everyone will make fun of you so you have to go along with professing how cool your car is even though you really don't think it is anymore.  So you are here now on this forum to find out more about Fieros so that you can find some reason for you to get one that won't make you look foolish.  Yet you still have to put up your front because your friend is on here.  Don't worry though we understand and we won't make fun of you when you are finally able to come out of the closet.  We will be more supportive and positive than any other group you have ever been a part of.  It will be ok when you deny this for we know that is just a sign of you hurting, lusting, longing for a Fiero.  And we will understand when you talk so well of your mustang for that is your heartache and morning for that Fiero that you could have had.  And we will be here when you are able to push away all of those things to become a Fiero ownner and know all of the joys that come with.  I wish only the best for you in these times to come, and I will be watching you lusting, longing and finally loving your Fiero after your long hard journey.  We love you man!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/tongue.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||Jefrysuko||10-25-2001||02:52 PM||||Just to keep this on topic.  I think I have done business with everyone mentioned and with more than positive results.  More needs to be said about Ed Parks though.  I called him once looking for parts and even though he didn't have anything he thought I would be satisfied with he spent a half hour telling me where I might find what I was looking for.  You kind of have to wonder how he stays in business without ever taking anyones money though  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000011||Galen||10-25-2001||03:27 PM||||Bought some lil doodads from Oreif, came quickly and he replaced one I broke cheaply  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> he rocks<P>------------------<BR><B>Ray</B> Webmaster of <A HREF="http://www.fierolinks.f2s.com/" TARGET=_blank>Fierolinks</A><BR>"The price of love is tragedy"||||reg||1
Z||000012||Old Lar||10-25-2001||04:15 PM||||I have purchased stuff from Kick Hill Farms, Twin Lakes Fiero, Fiero Parts and Apprasials, The Fiero Factory, Rodney Dickman, Fiero Store, FOCOA, Doug Kinney, fleabitdog, gmpartsdirect and have had all positive experiences.  Some others I've probably missed, sorry.  I've bought too much stuff.||||reg||1
Z||000013||Raydar||10-25-2001||04:22 PM||||Yeah, Ed Parks rocks!<BR>Ed and Rosy are two of the nicest people I've ever met. <BR>As was mentioned, Ed will go out of his way to help you, even if he doesn't stand to make any money. His advice is always free and based on years of experience.<P>Rodney's merchandise is always first rate, and he's always looking for new ideas to help us feed our addiction.<P>Anything that I've ever ordered from the Fiero Store was on my porch in 2-3 days.<P>The only thing I've ever bought from Doug Kinney was a used poly dogbone at the swap meet, but he's a helluva good guy, and I'm looking forward to buying a pair (or two) of side scoops from him. As soon as I clear out some of my clutter. <P>I'll also mention Don Hulse and Ashby Arnette.<BR>They are two "internet challenged" local guys that I have known for several years. They buy and part out (or restore) Fieros in the Atlanta area.<BR>They are both straight shooters. Take pride in what they sell. (Anyone who has bought a subwoofer system, or anything else, from an ad that I posted can attest to that.)<P><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000014||MinnGreenGT||10-25-2001||04:26 PM||||Hey! I had forgotten about Oreif too!  He sent my pieces out right away... I finally got around to installing them last weekend- they look fabulous!  Thanks Oreif!||||reg||1
Z||000015||Alex4mula||10-25-2001||04:45 PM||||This is cool! I'll save this thread and whenever I want to buy something from someone new I'll just look and make sure he was mentioned here  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red-Original Owner & White-1/94 with PM (:||||reg||1
Z||000016||BlackStang95||10-25-2001||05:09 PM||||Lol, man, I'm considering getting the Mustang horse logo with the red white and blue tri-bar behind it tatooed on my left shoulder someday.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I don't think I'll ever be trading the Stang in.  I would love one if I had some extra money lying around.  Anyone got an 84 2m4 they wanna get rid of?   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by BlackStang95 (edited 10-25-2001).]||||reg||6
Z||000017||FieroFanaticus2||10-25-2001||05:19 PM||||Gotta Be FieroDave!!<P>I bought the hoodscoop he was selling a while back.  Originally he was asking $200 I think.  When I talked to him on the phone he dropped it to $150.  Also while on the phone it turns out he has an extra driver's side front fender that I had been looking for, so add $25 for that.  Since I live in Wisconsin I figured I should just drive the 160 miles and pick up the parts myself.<P>When I got there I was pleasantly greeted and treated like a friend right away.  I got the hoodscoop - WITH THE HOOD INCLUDED and the Fender.  He asked if there were any other parts I was looking for and the only thing I could think of was a rear bumper cover, but told him that I would have to come back for that since I couldn't afford it at that time.  To my surprise he GAVE me one that had a small tear in it that was easily fixable.  He also lowered the cost of the hoodscoop to $125.  So, I got a rear bumper, a fender, and a hood with scoop included for $150.  And that's the day I met FieroDave.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000018||DXR_DAD||10-25-2001||05:25 PM||||Ok, I'll plug FieroDave and Rodney!!! Rodney sends those little flyers, and the business cards  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> I like that <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> he's fast and product is tops!!!!! fierodave, his stuff comes the same day!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> as i'm talking to him the package is on the way!!!( Oreif!!! thanks)<P>ALL of my dealing with forum members have been GOOD!! Buying & selling. I have seen how some of the vendors handle business here on the forum!! There are those that I will not deal with. There are those that have a great respect for their customers!!!!!and customer service, those are the ones that will last!<P>"Can you feel the love"<BR>DXR_DAD||||reg||14
